Freundlich gave an empirical relationship between the quantity of gas adsorbed by unit mass of solid adsorbent and concentration at a particular temperature.

\begin{aligned}
& \log x / m=\log K+\frac{1}{n} \log C \\
& x=\text { mass of gas adsorbed, } m=\text { mass of adsorbent } \\
& C=\text { concentration, } k, n=\text { constants. }
\end{aligned}
